      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Texas?",
      "a": "Texas received $77.3B in federal contract obligations during FY2026 to date. The state logged 158,566 awards with an average award size of $487K, and obligations were down 10.5% year over year. Fiscal-year totals for comparison are: FY21 $55.1B, FY22 $67.6B, FY23 $81.9B, FY24 $59.3B, and FY25 $86.3B."
